have you gone down the road of making  huge changes to your eating habits only  to find yourself failing over and over  again well the truth is making huge  changes and expecting quick results  isn't manageable and it may only work  short-term what we want to focus on is  to learn to make small manageable and  sustainable changes that will have a  huge impact long-term so I want to share  with you 15 really simple food swaps to  help you slash the calories without  making huge sacrifices to your favorite  food and flavors granola may sound like  a healthy breakfast option it might  shock you to know that just half a cup  of granola has about 300 calories it is  high in oil butter and sugar  so before muesli instead Loosli has the  same raw ingredients as granola but  without any oil butter or added sugar  you'll be saving about 156 calories a  chav ants latte with whole milk has an  average of 200 calories that's 10  percent of your daily calorie  recommendation shopping for a cup of  americano and you'll be saving 200  calories if it's too strong to your  liking you can always add a little bit  of semi skimmed milk Oh so before a cup  of green tea 1 tablespoon of mayo has a  whopping 90 4 calories and 10 grams of  fat it is high in calories but very low  in nutrients so before Greek yogurt  instead 1 tablespoon has 14 calories and  under 1 gram of fat you'll be saving 80  calories use it as salad dressing or  dips mix it with tuna eggs chicken a  potato or use it as the base of a creamy  dessert the dressing you choose may ruin  a healthy salad 1 tablespoon of creamy  salad dressing has a whopping 70  calories it's loaded with saturated fat  sugar and salt keep your salad healthy  and stop for oil and vinegar based  dressings instead you'll be saving 55  calories plus you'll be adding healthy  fats into your meal 1 small packet of  crisps has 170 calories and close to  zero nutrients they are  is saturated fats calories and salt so  pay for plain or lightly seasoned  air-popped popcorn one cup only has 31  calories it is packed with antioxidants  fiber and excellent for digestion don't  be fooled by soups one cup of creamy  mushroom soup can rack as many as 220  calories and 17 grams of fat shopping  for homemade broth base soup which is  just 18 calories per cup you'll be  saving more than 200 calories and also  your waist line a cup of whole dairy  milk has 148 calories stop before  unsweetened almond milk and save 88  calories almond milk is also great for  vegans of those with lactose intolerance  swap soda drinks including a diet soda  for sparkling water you will still get  the face of a can of soda but with other  chemicals colorings or artificial  sweeteners that can lead to weight gain  plus you get to meet your daily  requirement of drinking at least 2  liters of water 1 milli packet has about  416 calories if you want to reduce your  cup intake so before to medium sliced  breads you'll be saving about 236  calories or stop it for one medium  tortilla wrap and save 276 calories if  you want to go for a lower cup swap and  increase your vegetable intake then swap  the tortilla wrap for lettuce wrap  lettuce is also known as free food  because it's extremely low in calories  and you can read in abundance to fill  you up without piling on weight dried  fruits are high in nutrients and make  excellent healthy snack however if  you're watching your weight and want  more volume shopping for fresh fruits  instead a serving of fresh fruit offers  more volume and contains more water  which will keep your food quicker and  longer sugar is one of the top causes of  obesity across the world one teaspoon of  sugar contains 15 calories and no other  nutrients it is also very addictive  shopping for stevia stevia is a natural  sweetener and does not contain any  calories it is 300 times sweeter than  sugar  han-soo you only need a very small  amount to replace sugar it is also a  great sweet alternative for the  with diabetes a three and a half ounce  of dairy ice cream has 125 calories  seven grams of fat and 14 grams of sugar  the main ingredients are heavy cream and  egg yolks shopping for gelato instead  gelato uses more milk than cream and  fewer egg yolks a similar portion packs  in just 90 calories 3 grams of fat and  pang grams of sugar remember to still  indulge in moderation red meat is an  excellent source of protein and iron but  can be high in saturated fats consuming  too much of red meat can cause high  cholesterol and also cardiovascular  diseases limit red meat to once a week  and swap it for fish instead fish is  high in protein omega-3 but low in  calories and saturated fats desserts  tend to be very high in calories at a  400 calories per slice of cheesecake it  can contain more calories than your  dinner swap it for jell-o pudding  instead one serving has 150 calories  you'll be saving 250 calories plus your  efforts in the gym all these little food  swaps can add up to some huge calorie  savings start by practicing these really  simple food swaps and you will notice a  difference to your body and also how you  feel what other food swaps have you  tried to let me know in the comments  below so if you enjoyed this video if  you find this video to be helpful be  sure to give it a thumbs up share it  with your friends and do subscribe to my  youtube channel for new weekly videos do  also check out more video links in my  description box for more guides and tips  on healthy eating all the best  [Music]  you
 

